  "readmeFile": "NuGet.README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v2.1.4 (2026-11-13): quoted identifiers in CREATE TABLE are catalogued without their quoting, so a schema generated by a query builder (linq2db, EF Core, FluentMigrator) can insert into the table it just created, and ALTER TABLE ADD COLUMN reads a quoted column name the same way; Previous: v2.1.3 (2026-11-12): the linq2db adapter now executes on SharpCoreDB instead of SQLite, so a password is honoured and rows live in an encrypted SharpCoreDB file, and the SQL shapes that blocked it are fixed - pretty-printed INSERTs, SELECT-list projection, bare and negated boolean WHERE, LIKE with ESCAPE, scalar EXISTS, and hex byte[]/Guid literals. Previous: v2.1.2 (2026-10-26): patch release with no API changes - a bound text parameter is no longer re-scanned as SQL text, so a value holding an apostrophe, a doubled quote, a backslash, a comma or a parenthesis now round-trips exactly instead of landing in the neighbouring column or failing with \"Mismatched parentheses in VALUES clause\"; full detail in docs/CHANGELOG.md. Previous: v2.1.1 (2026-10-25): patch release with no API changes. A float[] parameter now reaches a VECTOR(n) column as a vector instead of the literal text \"System.Single[]\", and ORDER BY vec_distance_*() LIMIT k now reaches the vector index instead of a full scan. Previous: v2.1.0 (2026-10-10): net11.0-only (C# 15 preview) release line - 2,897 tests green across 16 suites; the fixed-width inline capacity ships at 16 by default on both storage paths (batched multi-row INSERT measured +12 to +19 percent); the overflow arena writes a row's payloads in one append instead of one file open per value; and in-place UPDATE/DELETE with deferred index maintenance put the fixed-width fair-PK layout ahead of SQLite on UPDATE (0.8x) and DELETE (0.5x). Full details: https://github.com/MPCoreDeveloper/SharpCoreDB/blob/master/docs/CHANGELOG.md",
